# Keep line endings consistent between your Windows machine and the Linux
# server this deploys to.
#
# Without this, Git rewrites every file's line endings on the way in and out,
# and you get pull requests where a hundred files "changed" and none of them
# actually did. Worse, a shell script with Windows line endings fails on Linux
# with a completely unhelpful error.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish things Git must not touch.
*.graphml -text
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
